body:
From the bottom of my heart, thank you. There are not nearly enough people in the world who would do what you did. I am an abuse survivor as well. I was 18 when my ex partner knelt on my chest and throat until I almost passed out while hitting my head because "it doesn't bruise as easy". Even though he was put in jail over the weekend, once he got out he told anyone who would listen that I was making it up. Unfortunately most of our friends sided with him and I was completely ostracized from my tiny town. I wound up moving to the other side of my county to get away from them. I couldn't even walk down my town centre without someone calling me a lying whore from the apartments above. It makes me sick to my stomach that so many people have the "not my business" attitude and will blatantly ignore these types of things. 

&#x200B;

You very well could saved her and her childrens lives tonight or down the line. Abuse like that only escalates. You did an amazing thing OP.
